{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2920","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2920","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2920\",\"parent_revision\":\"96ae7bbb3eaa4e93ed46228d6b3fc6108762a98c\",\"root_revision\":\"bd3e939273097cc2df8006d07bf508f99862c3e2f7fae0c0f1f4fe7253f61b41\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_contents.py` contains three separate code paths that each independently handle a GitHub API write-conflict (409/422) response: `_content_branch()` (branch-ref creation), `put()` (content writes), and `create_integration_branch()` (a related git-ref creation path elsewhere in the same file). These have diverged over time \u2014 `create_integration_branch()` raises unconditionally on a 422 with no re-verification, `_content_branch()` was recently changed (PR #2918, commit d84c666f) to re-verify branch existence after a 422 before trusting it, and `put()` has its own separate established re-read pattern. There is no shared abstraction reconciling the three.\\n\\nThis was surfaced during PR #2918's review-and-fix cycle (2026-08-16/17): a real bug (`_content_branch()` trusting a 422 conflict without re-verification, silently marking a branch \\\"ready\\\" that was never created) was found and fixed in one of the three paths. The review that found it did not check whether `create_integration_branch()` has the same failure mode \u2014 it has not been independently audited against it.\\n\\nSeparately, the same review cycle surfaced maintainability symptoms in the same file and its tests: the `_Repository` test fake in `tests/test_github_contents.py` has duplicated call-tracking state, the code comment above `_CONTENT_BRANCH` now duplicates prose already present in `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `list_all`/`get_many` share a duplicated tree-fetch code block.\\n\\nWhere observed: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github_contents.py` and its test file, during PR #2918's fix cycle.\\n\\nImpact: without auditing or reconciling the three conflict-handling paths against one another, a future fix to one of them (as happened with `_content_branch()` in PR #2918) risks leaving the others' identical bug class unaddressed \u2014 increasing both bug-recurrence risk and ongoing review/maintenance cost from reading three divergent implementations of what is conceptually one operation.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **simplify github_contents.py: shared-helper extraction and test-fake cleanup** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #2918 review follow-up\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"eab0e0a237d5bb94da2a3a9a84ceaaae90e42e41da12b7af8f0e8f2c72126530\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg7HdQ\"}"}